keywords:
  - AI security
  - coding agents
  - large language models
  - backdoors
  - code review
  - security audit
abstract: >-
  AI coding agents recognize the backdoors they read, but they read only what
  they judge relevant. Twelve working backdoors in Gitea and Jenkins were found
  in 43 of 48 single-backdoor reviews by GPT-6.1 Sol and Opus 5.5. Tool traces
  show that the agents read a median of 8.5% of the lines and explained the
  backdoor in 90 of 93 cases in which its decisive line appeared in their tool
  output, but in none of 24 cases in which it did not. Hidden in Plain Code
  (HIPC) turns these reading habits into rules for backdoors that look not
  worth reading. HIPC backdoors were found in full in only 3 of 21 reviews.
